<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Open Source Licenses — Budget Planner</title>
    <meta name="description" content="License text for every open-source component Budget Planner is built from, including its five on-device models.">
    <link rel="icon" href="favicon.ico" sizes="any">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0f1720">
    <style>
        :root { color-scheme: dark; }
        body {
            margin: 0;
            background: #0f1720;
            color: #e6edf3;
            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
            line-height: 1.65;
        }
        main { max-width: 40rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 48px 20px 80px; }
        h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin: 0 0 4px; }
        h2 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 36px 0 8px; }
        h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 28px 0 4px; }
        h4 { font-size: 0.85rem; margin: 12px 0 4px; color: #9fb0c2; font-weight: 600; }
        p, li { color: #c6d2df; }
        a { color: #7ee787; }
        .updated { color: #8b9bad; font-size: 0.85rem; margin: 0 0 32px; }
        .licenses-overview, .licenses-list, .license-used-by {
            list-style-type: none;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }
        .note { color: #9fb0c2; font-size: 0.9rem; }
        .licenses-overview li { display: inline-block; margin: 0 12px 6px 0; }
        .license-used-by li { display: inline-block; margin: 0 10px 4px 0; font-size: 0.9rem; }
        .license { border-top: 1px solid #223; padding-top: 4px; }
        /* The model table has three columns of real prose, which does not
           fit a 375px phone. Let it scroll sideways inside its own box
           rather than widening the page. Same treatment as privacy.html. */
        .models-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin: 12px 0; }
        table.models { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; min-width: 34rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
        table.models th, table.models td {
            text-align: left;
            vertical-align: top;
            padding: 8px 12px 8px 0;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #223;
            color: #c6d2df;
        }
        table.models th { color: #e6edf3; font-weight: 600; }
        /* The license texts are long and there are dozens of them; a scroll
           box keeps the page navigable without hiding anything. `pre-wrap`
           matters more than it looks — these texts are hard-wrapped at 80
           columns, which overflows a 375px phone without it. */
        .license-text {
            max-height: 240px;
            overflow-y: auto;
            white-space: pre-wrap;
            font-size: 0.8rem;
            background: #131c26;
            border: 1px solid #223;
            border-radius: 8px;
            padding: 12px 14px;
            color: #c6d2df;
        }
        footer { margin-top: 48px; border-top: 1px solid #223; padding-top: 16px; font-size: 0.85rem; }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
    <main>
        <h1>Open Source Licenses</h1>
        <p class="updated">Generated by <code>cargo about</code> from this app's own dependency graph.</p>

        <p>
            Budget Planner is built from open-source software. Most of it is
            compiled into the WebAssembly engine your browser downloads, which
            makes that file a binary distribution of every project listed
            below — and their licenses ask that their copyright notices travel
            with it. This page is where those notices travel. Nothing here is
            a network service; none of it sees a figure you type.
        </p>

        <h2>Machine-learning models</h2>
        <p>
            The five models behind receipt scanning and voice entry are not
            Cargo dependencies, so they are listed by hand rather than
            generated. Four were converted to the <code>rten</code> runtime's
            own file format and all-MiniLM-L6-v2 ships as the ONNX file it was
            downloaded as; in neither case does anything change about the
            model's architecture or its trained weights. See
            <a href="https://github.com/dengf/budget_planner/blob/main/MODEL-LICENSES.md">MODEL-LICENSES.md</a>
            for the fuller record, including the copyright line each project
            asks to be carried.
        </p>
        <div class="models-wrap">
        <table class="models">
            <thead>
                <tr><th>Model</th><th>Used for</th><th>License</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><a href="https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR">PP-OCRv6_tiny</a></td>
                    <td>Reading text off a photographed receipt</td>
                    <td><a href="#Apache-2.0">Apache-2.0</a></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><a href="https://huggingface.co/Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2">all-MiniLM-L6-v2</a></td>
                    <td>Income or expense, for an unsigned statement row</td>
                    <td><a href="#Apache-2.0">Apache-2.0</a></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><a href="https://catalog.ngc.nvidia.com/orgs/nvidia/nemo/models/stt_en_quartznet15x5">QuartzNet15x5</a></td>
                    <td>English speech-to-text</td>
                    <td>© NVIDIA, NeMo toolkit</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><a href="https://catalog.ngc.nvidia.com/orgs/nvidia/teams/nemo/models/stt_zh_citrinet_512">Citrinet-512</a></td>
                    <td>Mandarin speech-to-text</td>
                    <td>© NVIDIA, NeMo toolkit</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><a href="https://huggingface.co/ASLP-lab/WSYue-ASR">u2pp-Conformer-Yue</a></td>
                    <td>Cantonese speech-to-text</td>
                    <td><a href="#Apache-2.0">Apache-2.0</a></td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
        </div>
        <p>
            PP-OCRv6_tiny is © 2020 PaddlePaddle Authors. u2pp-Conformer-Yue
            is © ASLP-lab, Northwestern Polytechnical University, trained on
            WenetSpeech-Yue (arXiv:2509.03959). The Apache-2.0 text those
            three are licensed under is reproduced in full below, under
            <a href="#Apache-2.0">Apache-2.0</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Rust crates — overview</h2>
        <ul class="licenses-overview">
            {{#each overview}}
            <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
            {{/each}}
        </ul>

        <h2>Rust crates — full license text</h2>
        <p class="note">
            A license appears once per distinct copyright notice, so the same
            license shows up several times with a different "Used by" list
            each time — that repetition is the point, since it is the
            copyright lines, not the license body, that each project asks to
            have carried.
        </p>
        <ul class="licenses-list">
            {{#each licenses}}
            <li class="license">
                <h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>
                <h4>Used by:</h4>
                <ul class="license-used-by">
                    {{#each used_by}}
                    <li><a href="{{#if crate.repository}}{{crate.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}{{/if}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
                    {{/each}}
                </ul>
                <pre class="license-text">{{text}}</pre>
            </li>
            {{/each}}
        </ul>

        <footer>
            <a href="./">&larr; Back to the calculator</a>
            &nbsp;·&nbsp;
            <a href="privacy.html">Privacy policy</a>
        </footer>
    </main>
</body>

</html>
